# v0.24.17 — Canonical 0x address migration and final fixes

## AITBC MCP server update (2026-08-26)

- Expanded `ALL_AITBC_GROUPS` to include the newly shipped Phase 6 CLI groups:
  `agent`, `dashboard`, `ipfs`, `marketplace`, and `system`.
- Updated `ALL_SERVICE_ENDPOINTS` and `ALL_SERVICE_BASES` with the new
  island IPFS (`aitbc-island-ipfs`), Whisper (`aitbc-whisper`), FFmpeg
  (`aitbc-ffmpeg`), and Ollama (`ollama`) endpoints.
- Added typed MCP tools wrapping the new daily-use commands:
  - `check_aitbc_system_health`
  - `list_aitbc_ipfs_rentals`
  - `list_aitbc_ipfs_pins`
  - `get_aitbc_agent_status`
  - `get_aitbc_agent_inbox`
  - `get_aitbc_dashboard_customer`
  - `get_aitbc_dashboard_shop`
- fix(miner,coordinator): aitbc-miner heartbeats now report status: ONLINE so the coordinator counts it in the online pool; coordinator dispatch and online-count now ignore miners whose last heartbeat is older than COORDINATOR_MINER_HEARTBEAT_CUTOFF_SECONDS (default 5 min)
- fix(miner): map marketplace/CLI job types (ollama, llama, whisper, ffmpeg) to the worker inference/transcribe/reencode handlers
- feat(mcp): add manage_ai_job tool for accept/cancel/refund AI jobs
- fix(mcp): run_aitbc_cli options now accept null for boolean flags
- feat(mcp): whitelist bridge, exchange, exchange-island, explorer, gpu, governance CLI groups
- feat(coordinator): add background StaleMinerReaper to mark stale ONLINE miners OFFLINE
- ops(hub): create island credentials and validate exchange-island orderbook/rates
- ops(hub): stop orphaned aitbc-pool-hub process (canonical pool-hub remains on aitbc3)

## Canonical 0x address migration and live chain reset (2026-08-27)

- feat(address): canonical EIP-55 0x secp256k1/EVM address migration across core,
  CLI, wallet, bridge, marketplace, tests, docs, website, and MCP wrappers
  (commit `7774d37f7` on gitea `main`).
- feat(genesis): `init_production_genesis.py` and production setup scripts now
  write canonical 0x addresses into `genesis_prod.yaml` and blockchain `.env`.
- fix(state): `compute_state_root_full()` reads raw SQL and recomputes the trie
  deterministically after DB mutations.
- ops: live reset of the `ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net` chain on `hub.aitbc`,
  `aitbc3`, and `hub2.aitbc`:
  - Backed up `/var/lib/aitbc/data/ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net`.
  - Migrated `/etc/aitbc/*.env` and `/var/lib/aitbc/wallets/*.json` to 0x.
  - Regenerated `genesis.json` with a deterministic genesis block and state root.
  - All three nodes converged to height 4 with matching block hashes.
  - Wallet send round-trip from `genesis` to `default` succeeded and balances
    matched across all RPC nodes.
- fix(ops): migrated `keystore.db` and `wallet_ledger.db` metadata from legacy
  `ait1`/`aitbc1` to canonical `0x` on `hub.aitbc` and `aitbc3`.
